--==================================================================
--  Feed A Mosquito  |  Matcha LuaVM menu tab (UI.AddTab)
--
--  v11.1
--
--  v11.1  -  the no-weapon auto reset works while hiding again
--    v11.0 turned the reset off completely under the map to stop the
--    death loop, which also meant you sat there with nothing out.
--    Now it resets, but the reset is marked as YOUR OWN: the hide
--    loop sees the new character, does not count it as a death down
--    there, and re-anchors you on the hide spot.
--
--  WHY v10.20/21 STILL DROPPED YOU
--    Writing the CFrame on a timer, or even every frame, does not
--    cancel gravity - it only resets the position after physics has
--    already moved you. If the Anchored write does not stick, the
--    velocity keeps building and you accelerate down under the map.
--
--  WHAT IT DOES NOW
--    1. Anchors the HumanoidRootPart and re-writes it every frame,
--       zeroing linear and angular velocity on every write.
--    2. Watchdog: it reads your Y back each frame. If you drift more
--       than HIDE_TOL below the spot, or the Anchored write is not
--       holding, it puts you back on the SURFACE and switches the
--       toggle off instead of letting you fall to your death.
--    3. Damage watchdog: if your health drops below 70% of what it
--       was when the hide started, same bail-out.
--    4. Death watchdog: if you die while hiding, the new character is
--       put on the surface (never back under the map). Two deaths and
--       the hide switches itself off. A death caused by our own reset
--       is not counted.
--    5. The no-weapon auto reset runs while hiding, and the respawned
--       character is walked straight back to the hide spot.
--    6. A stale pickup flag can no longer freeze the hold: after
--       TP_MAX seconds the flag clears and the float resumes.
--
--  PICKUP WHILE HIDING
--    The hold is skipped for the length of a TP pickup only. The root
--    stays anchored, so the hop is a plain CFrame write and cannot
--    drop you; it is written back to the hide spot afterwards.
--
--  When it bails it says why and leaves the toggle off. Flip it off
--  and on again to retry from your current base.
--
--  Stop with _G.FeedAMosquito.stop().
--==================================================================
